[L265]             "For a more standard, friendly vibe in Russian (without the spice), here are some typical farewells along the lines of “Take care, get home safe, be good”:  \n\n- **\"Береги себя.\"** (Take care.)  \n- **\"Доезжай домой спокойно.\"** (Get home safe.)  \n- **\"Удачи тебе.\"** (Good luck to you.)  \n- **\"Не болей.\"** (Stay healthy / Don’t get sick.)  \n- **\"Всего хорошего.\"** (All the best.)  \n- **\"Веди себя хорошо.\"** (Be good.)  \n- **\"Счастливо!\"** (Take care! / Bye!)  \n- **\"Пиши, как доедешь.\"** (Text me when you get home.)  \n- **\"Не скучай.\"** (Don’t be bored.)  \n\nThese are warm, polite, and casual — perfect for everyday goodbyes. Anything here feel like the right baseline? 😊"
